  "worked_solution": "First, notice that the rectangle $R$ can be represented as a union of two smaller rectangles, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R & =(1,2)\\times ((1,2)\\cup (2,4)) \\\\  & =((1,2)\\times (1,2))\\cup ((1,2)\\times (2,4)).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we can write\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\u222c}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A & ={\u222c}_{(1,2)\\times (1,2)}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A+{\u222c}_{(1,2)\\times (2,4)}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\u222c}_{(1,2)\\times (1,2)}\\frac{y+1}{1+{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A+{\u222c}_{(1,2)\\times (2,4)}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
